  "steps": [
    "Place the ham flat side down on a roasting rack in a roasting pan and pour 1 cup pineapple juice into the bottom of the pan.",
    "Mix the melted butter and hot honey and brush it all over the ham and between the slices.",
    "Cover with foil and bake at 275°F for 8 minutes per pound, about 1 hour 30 minutes for an 11 lb ham.",
    "Meanwhile, mix both sugars with the seasoned salt, garlic powder, cinnamon, nutmeg, cloves, ginger, paprika and allspice, then divide into 3 equal bowls.",
    "Take the ham out, set the oven to broil on high, and reserve 3 tbsp of the pan drippings.",
    "Pat the first bowl of sugar mixture over the ham, working it into the crevices, and broil uncovered for 2 minutes.",
    "Pat on the second bowl and broil another 2 minutes.",
    "Reserve 1 cup of the pan drippings. Simmer them in a saucepan with the last bowl of sugar mixture, soy sauce, vinegar and Dijon until it boils, then remove from the heat.",
    "Brush the glaze all over the ham and broil 2 to 3 minutes until bubbly and crisp. Slice and serve with the pan juices."
  ],
